 compare the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-class to other vehicles you're interest\", 'images': [], 'rank': 1}, {'url': 'https://www.kbb.com/mercedes-benz/s-class/2025/specs/', 'content': \"2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Specs & Feature Comparisons | Kelley Blue Book Car Values Price New/Used My Car's Value Instant Cash Offer Cars for Sale Cars for Sale Free Dealer Price Quote Vehicle History Report Find Local Dealers Private Seller Exchange Private Seller Cars Sell Your Car Shop & Buy Best Cars Dealer Reviews KBB Expert Reviews Electric Vehicle Guide KBB Awards Latest Car News Shopping & Buying Research Tools Car Research Browse Incentives Car Loan Calculator Car Finder Compare Cars Car Loans Insurance Check My Credit Extended Warranty Vehicle History Report Car Repair Auto Repair Prices Car Recalls Maintenance Pricing Find an Auto Shop Service Advisor OBD-II Codes Home Mercedes-Benz Mercedes-Benz S-Class Specs and Features 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Specs, Features & Options Here's everything you need to know about each trim in the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class lineup. Compare pricing, specs, key features and more. More About the 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-class 1 of 3 S-Class S 500 4MATIC 2 of 3 S-Class S 580e 4MATIC 3 of 3 S-Class S 580 4MATIC See Pricing See Cars in Stock See Pricing See Cars in Stock See Pricing See Cars in Stock Save 1 of 3 S-Class S 500 4MATIC Save 2 of 3 S-Class S 580e 4MATIC Save 3 of 3 S-Class S 580 4MATIC See Pricing See Cars in Stock See Pricing See Cars in Stock See Pricing See Cars in Stock MSRP $118,900 $129,350 $129,750 Fuel Economy City 21/Hwy 31/Comb 24 MPG Comb 23 MPG City 18/Hwy 27/Comb 21 MPG Fuel Type Gas Hybrid LeafIcon Gas Horsepower 442 HP 510 @ 5500 RPM 496 HP Engine 6-Cyl, MHEV, Turbo, 3.0 Liter 6-Cyl, Hybrid, Turbo, 3.0 Liter V8, MHEV, Twin Turbo, 4.0 Liter Cargo Volume 12.90 cu ft 12.90 cu ft 12.90 cu ft Cylinders 6 6 8 Torque 413 lb-ft 694 lb-ft 516 lb-ft 0 - 60 4.9 seconds 4.5 seconds 4.3 seconds Curb Weight 4,740 pounds 5,501 pounds 4,784 pounds Safety Features Blind-Spot Alert Standard Standard Standard Collision Warning System Standard Standard Standard Driver Attention Assist Monitor Standard Standard Standard Child Seat Anchors Standard Standard Standard Child Door Locks Standard Standard Standard Traction Control Standard Standard Standard Surround View Camera Standard Standard Standard Technology Bluetooth Wireless Technology Standard Standard Standard Cruise Control Standard Standard Standard Remote Keyless Entry Standard Standard Standard Remote Engine Start Standard Standard Standard Smartphone Interface Standard Standard Standard Internet Access Standard Standard Standard Proximity Sensing Keyless Entry Standard Standard Standard Navigation System Standard Standard Standard Voice Recognition System Standard Standard Standard Touch Screen Monitor Standard Standard Standard Hands Free Phone Standard Standard Standard Entertainment Premium Radio Standard Standard Standard Bluetooth Streaming Audio Standard Standard Standard Bluetooth Wireless Technology Standard Standard Standard Satellite Radio Standard Standard Standard Comfort & Convenience Remote Keyless Entry Standard Standard Standard Cruise Control Standard Standard Standard Bluetooth Streaming Audio Standard Standard Standard Heated Mirrors Standard Standard Standard Heated Steering Wheel Optional Standard Not Available Integrated Garage Door Opener Standard Standard Standard Performance Torque 413 foot pounds 694 @ 5500 RPM 516 foot pounds 0 to 60 4.9 seconds 4.5 seconds 4.3 seconds Top Speed 130 mph 130 mph 130 mph Estimated Electric Range Not Available 48 miles Not Available Seating Leather Seats Standard Standard Standard Dual Power Front Seats Standard Standard Standard Power Driver's Seat Standard Standard Standard Interior Leather-Wrapped Steering Wheel Standard Standard Standard Power Outlet Standard Standard Standard Power Windows Standard Standard Standard Rear Window Defroster Standard Standard Standard Steering Wheel Controls Standard Standard Standard Tilt Steering Wheel Standard Standard Standard Tilt/Telescoping Steering Wheel Standard Standard Standard Cup Holder Count Standard Standard Standard\", 'images': [], 'rank': 2}, {'url': 'https://www.carsdirect.com/mercedes-benz/s-class/2025', 'content': 'New Cars | Used Cars | New Car Deals | Auto Loans | Research & News Mercedes-Benz Mercedes-Benz S-Class 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Mercedes-Benz S-Class 2025  GO 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Photos Colors Price Range $118,900 - $241,650 Expert Rating Coming Soon Get a Price Quote Build & Price Your Car New 2025 Used 2024 2023 2022 2021 More Years OverviewPrices & Deals Specs & Features Compare Cars Generations Overview By Neil Cumins  Automotive Editor Dec 11, 2024 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Changes There are no significant changes to Mercedes Benzs sedan flagship for 2025, other than new paint colors and a standard digital key. This remains a four-engine range, with prices starting at around $120,000. Choosing Your 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Mercedes-Benz doesnt offer anything as common as trim levels, so your choice of S-Class revolves around which powertrain youd like. The base S 500 4MATIC will set you back $118,900, while the plug-in hybrid 580e costs $129,350. The biturbo 580 is $400 more expensive, while the AMG S 63 E has a price tag as hefty as its performance it costs $187,350. 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Engine Options The 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class engine range starts with a three-liter inline-6 turbo. In its standard form, it generates 442 horsepower and 413 lb-ft of torque, while the plug-in hybrid variant produces 503 hp and 553 lb-ft. Performance is enhanced in the S 580 with a four-liter V8 biturbo, generating 496 hp and 516 lb-ft, though the AMG blows these figures away by combining the bigger engine with a 150kW electric motor to produce 791 hp and a frankly stunning 1,055 lb-ft. Every S-Class is AWD and deploys a nine-speed automatic transmission. Engine Type\\tHorsepower\\tTorque 3.0 turbo\\t442 hp\\t413 lb-ft 3.0 turbo plug-in hybrid\\t503 hp\\t553 lb-ft 4.0 V8 biturbo\\t496 hp\\t516 lb-ft 4.0 V8 biturbo hybrid\\t791 hp\\t1,055 lb-ft 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Fuel Economy 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class fuel economy stands at an EPA-estimated 21 miles per gallon city, 31 mpg highway, and 24 combined in base S 500 guise. Gas mileage drops in the 580 gas model to 17/25/20 MPG, while figures for the PHEV and AMG versions hadnt been published at the time of writing. 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Towing Capacity Given its luxury orientation, Mercedes-Benz has decided not to quote towing capacities for the S-Class. 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Dimensions & Cargo Capacity 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class dimensions include an overall length of 208 inches, generating 41 and 44 inches of front and rear legroom. 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class cargo space stands at 13 cu ft with the rear seats in place. 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Safety Given its premium status, its unsurprising that the S-Class is imbued with a wealth of standard safety features. There are nine airbags including a front center bag, a dashcam, surround-view cameras, and ultra-wide high beams built into the intelligent LED lighting. Driver aids include torque vectoring braking, active and evasive steering assistance, active blind-spot assistance, and automatic lane changing. AMG models up the ante further with facial recognition and an augmented reality head-up display. 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Technology For decades, the S-Class has led the passenger car market in terms of technology, and the latest generation model wants for nothing. Youll find biometric authentication and voice control with natural language understanding in every model. A 12.3-inch digital instrument cluster joins a 12.8-inch OLED touchscreen display with navigation, satellite/HD radio, and a Burmester 3D surround sound system incorporating Dolby Atmos. If you want to take your music to another dimension, a 4D system is available on all models with seat-integrated resonators and 30 speakers. 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class Trims & Prices 2025 Mercedes-Benz S-Class MSRP from $118,900 Build & Price > From the LED logo projectors to the soft-closing doors with their illuminated sills, everything abou', 'images': [], 'rank': 3}, {'url': 'https://www.autoguide.com/Mercedes-Benz/S-Class', 'content': \"Join Now Top stories Run As Fast As You Can From Used Cars Made By These Brands Top 5 Longest Lasting Trucks Join a Community of Car Lovers and Subscribe to Our YouTube Channel Manufacturers Hybrids Mercedes-Benz S-Class Review, Specs, Pricing, Features, Videos and More by AutoGuide.com Staff Updated: February 14th, 2023 Share Find everything you need to know about the Mercedes-Benz S-Class here, along with expert reviews, specs, photos, videos and more. Price\\t$111,100 - $122,550 Engine\\t3.0-liter turbo 6-cylinder + hybrid / 4.0-liter turbo 8-cylinder + hybrid / 3.0-liter turbo 6-cylinder + plug-in hybrid Power\\t429 hp / 496 hp / 510 hp Torque\\t384 lb-ft. / 516 lb-ft. / 553 lb-ft. Drivetrain\\tAWD CHECK BEST PRICE Mercedes-Benz flagship sedan is one of the most luxurious four-doors out there. Dripping with elegance, the S-Class continues to be a standard in the segment. Recently, a plug-in hybrid version joined the lineup, utilizing a turbocharged six-cylinder engine and electric motors. Every S-Class now comes standard with 4Matic all-wheel drive and a nine-speed automatic transmission. Buttery smooth to drive, the S-Class is meant for rear seat passengers as much as those up front. Table of contents 2021 Mercedes-Benz S580 Review: Flagship Sets the Bar Competitors Detailed Specs 2021 Mercedes-Benz S580 Review: Flagship Sets the Bar The S-Class has never been just the Mercedes flagship. Its also a crystal ball. Thats what makes the 2021 Mercedes-Benz S580 such an important car to test: it gives us a taste of the tech well see trickle down through the rest of the industry over the next decade. Here at the end of 2021, the S-Class also reminds us of the power of big luxury sedans. You can roll up to any fancy event in one of the myriad high-end SUVs these days, but you arrive in an S-Class. The ninth generation of Mercs flagship still oozes class and comfort, yet it mixes in more tech and surprisingly agile responses, all without upsetting the equilibrium thats made this the standard of the class for decades. Mercedes has developed an entirely new platform for the S-Class, one thats stronger yet also lighter. Its larger, too, though only slightly. This is the long-wheelbase version, which is the only length of regular S-Class youll find in America. The extra-spendy Maybach stretches longer still, while Canada has a short-wheelbase S500. This Goldilocks Sonderklasse still measures nearly 208 inches (5,280 mm) tip to taillonger than a GLS, with an extra 2.8 inches (70 mm) between the axles, too. Click Here to Read the Review Competitors Audi A8 BMW 7 Series Genesis G90 Lexus LS Detailed Specs Price\\t$111,100 - $122,550 Engine\\t3.0-liter turbo 6-cylinder + hybrid / 4.0-liter turbo 8-cylinder + hybrid / 3.0-liter turbo 6-cylinder + plug-in hybrid Power\\t429 hp / 496 hp / 510 hp Torque\\t384 lb-ft. / 516 lb-ft. / 553 lb-ft. Drivetrain\\tAWD Transmission\\t9AT Fuel Economy (city/hwy)\\t16-21 mpg / 25-30 mpg / plug-in TBD Cargo Capacity\\t12.9 cu ft. Print Recent Articles The Alpine A290 Rallye is the EV Race Car We Want Ariel Atom Gets 525 hp Anniversary Special Fourth of July: The 10 Most Iconic American Cars 2025 Acura ADX A-Spec Review: Filling the Gap Ford Mustang - Review, Specs, Pricing, Features, Videos and More Fiat Announces 500 Hybrid With Six-Speed Manual Transmission People Are Really Happy With The Quality Of These SUVs AutoGuide.com Staff More by AutoGuide.com Staff Autoguide Insurance Comments Sign Up to Comment Dash Cam Buyer's Guide Insurance Hub Get Answers Popular Articles Why You Should Never Drive Your Car On Empty Calling All Third