 and high owner satisfaction ratings. The 2020 and 2021 models have also demonstrated impressive reliability, thanks to advanced technology and solid build quality. The least reliable years for the Mercedes-Benz S-Class include 1999-2006, 2007, and 2014, due to issues with suspension, rust, transmission, and overheating. Common problems with the S-Class include rusting, airmatic suspension system failures, electrical issues, and water leaking into the interior. The W220 generation (2000-2006) is considered the most problematic, with numerous reliability issues and a low HC Rating of 3.3/10. Most Reliable Years for the Mercedes-Benz S-Class Vehicle In terms of the Mercedes-Benz S-Class , youll want to opt for models that have proven themselves to be reliable over the years . The 2009 and 2012 models stand out for their exceptional reliability, with few reported issues and high owner satisfaction ratings. More recently, the 2020 and 2021 models have also demonstrated impressive reliability, thanks to advanced technology and solid build quality. These reliable years offer a hassle-free ownership experience, with low maintenance costs averaging around $1,200 annually, making them an attractive choice for those seeking a dependable luxury sedan. General Reliability and Maintenance Costs Youll be relieved to know that the Mercedes-Benz S-Class line is generally reliable, making it a great choice for those seeking a dependable luxury vehicle. In terms of maintenance , you can expect to pay around $1,200 annually , although this cost can vary depending on the specific model and year you own. As you consider your options, its essential to factor in these costs and research how different model years compare in relation to reliability and maintenance needs. Reliability Overview The Mercedes-Benz S-Class line of vehicles boasts a reputation for being fairly reliable , especially when compared to similar low-cost luxury sedans. You can expect a used S-Class to be an excellent choice if you want a reliable vehicle with various high-end features . The S-Class has a good reliability record , but maintenance can be expensive, especially for complex systems like the air suspension and electrical system. Annual Maintenance Cost Your Mercedes-Benz S-Classs maintenance costs can add up quickly, but knowing what to expect helps you budget accordingly. On average , you can expect to pay around $1,200 per year for\', \'images\': [], \'rank\': 2}, {\'url\': \'https://www.parkers.co.uk/mercedes-benz/s-class/review/mpg-running-costs/\', \'content\': "Mercedes-Benz S-Class (2025) mpg, costs & reliability Primary Navigation Mobile Close menu Cars Vans & Pickups Saved Cars Reviews New car reviews Used car reviews New Car Awards Car companies Electric cars SUV Cars Owner reviews Extended reviews For sale Used cars for sale New cars for sale Nearly new cars for sale Car history check Car choosing tool Valuations Free car valuation Sell my car Leasing & Finance Car Leasing Car leasing special offers Car leasing advice Car Finance Car finance advice Get finance quote Car loan calculator Car specs Car Tax Car Tax advice Car advice Best Cars Best car products Car buying Car glossary Used cars Car news Car comparison Car Jargon Explained Company cars Car tax calculator How benefit-in-kind BIK tax works Insurance Buy a car warranty Compare car insurance Find a car\'s insurance group GAP insurance Car insurance advice Menu Cars Vans & Pickups Saved Cars More from Parkers Reviews New car reviews Used car reviews New Car Awards Car companies Electric cars SUV Cars Owner reviews Extended reviews For sale Used cars for sale New cars for sale Nearly new cars for sale Car history check Car choosing tool Valuations Free car valuation Sell my car Leasing & Finance Car Leasing Car leasing special offers Car leasing advice Car Finance Car finance advice Get finance quote Car loan calculator Car specs Car Tax Car Tax advice Car advice Best Cars Best car products Car buying Ca