 automatic gearboxes were the 7g tiptronic plus and both had periodic niggles with confused changes. The food news is a software upgrade and periodic resets, which can be done by the driver following a very simple series of steps, puts this right. Would I recommend the car? I have had a lot of E Class deisel cars over the years. If you are prepared to look after them properly they won\\'t let you down. They do lose a lot of residual value from new, but most luxury cars seem to. There are few cars that make the owner feel quite as special as a MB. Would you recommend the car to a friend? Yes Read more 5 out of 5 Car Details Model E Class 220d AMG Line Premium Plus 4dr 9G-Tronic Year 2018 Avg annual mileage 10,000 14,999 Owned Less than a year Bought Car Used Typical MPG 48 Tell us what you think about your car? This is my sixth Mercedes E Class and is the best by far. Has a superb comfortable ride even on run flat tyres, good fuel consumption I\\'m averaging 48 mpg since taking to the road. On long weekend journeys to Wales from Brackley I average over 50 mpg at average journey speed of 60 mph. A round day trip is 360 miles in superb silent luxury. Would you recommend the car to a friend? Yes Read more 5 out of 5 Car Details Model 220d SE Premium Year 2016 Avg annual mileage 5,000 9,999 Owned Less than a year Bought Car New Typical MPG 55 Tell us what you think about your car? I must say this is the best car I have ever owned. The tech is awesome, I\\'m really enjoying the widescreen cockpit. The car handles well and gives great mileage on fuel. The ride is smooth I chose the SE as the AMG comes with runflat tyres. I also believe the SE on standard 17 wheels offers a smoother ride. Would you recommend the car to a friend? Yes Read more E-Class Executive cars Family cars Cars E-Class saloon Share on Facebook Share on Twitter Share on LinkedIn Share via Email Recommended Top 10 best motorway cars 2025 Best cars 16 Apr 2025 16 Apr 2025 Top 10 best motorway cars 2025 The new Audi A6 saloon has finally landed, and costs from just over 50k News 15 Apr 2025 15 Apr 2025 The new', 'images': [], 'rank': 1}, {'url': 'https://www.whatcar.com/mercedes-benz/e-class/saloon/used-review/n17423/reliability', 'content': \"Used Mercedes E-Class - 2016-2024 Reliability & Common Problems | What Car? Reviews New car reviews Used car reviews Long-term reviews Accessibility & Motability New car deals Car deals Cars available now Leasing Leasing deals Leasing guides Used cars for sale News & advice Latest stories Advice Cost of living advice Company car news & advice Leasing advice Best of Top 10s Car comparisons Reliability New car awards Used car awards Electric car awards Van awards Tools & services All motoring services Sell my car Value my car Finance car Real MPG Company car tax calculator Fuel comparison tool Vans Commercial vans Lifestyle vans Van tax calculator Van awards Electric Company car Search more than 20,000 new cars in stock now >> Home Mercedes Used Mercedes E-Class 2016-2024 Reliability Used Mercedes E-Class 2016-2024 reliability Category: Luxury car The Mercedes E-Class is elegant, classy, well-equipped and good to drive, and greatvalue used. 1 What is it like? 2 Ownership cost 3 Our recommendations 4 Alternatives 5 Reliability Open Gallery Used Mercedes E-Class 2016-2024 review Star rating See used cars for sale Finance this car by Mark Pearson Updated 25 January 2022 How we test cars Used Cars for sale Mercedes-Benz E Class 2.1 E220 BlueTEC SE G-Tronic+ Euro 6 (s/s) 4dr 2016 7,195 Mercedes-Benz E Class 2.1 E220 BlueTEC AMG Night Edition G-Tronic+ Euro 6 (s/s) 4dr 2016 7,899 View all used car deals What should I look for in a used Mercedes E-Class saloon? Check the exterior of the car carefully for any scuffs and dents; the E-Class is a surprisingly long car that may well have been used in tight car parks. Make sure all electrical equipment works as it should. Also check the alloy wheels for any kerb damage. What are the most common problems with a used Mercedes E-Class saloon? The engine may lose power Due to an engine management software issue, examples built from the start of production to 31 May 2016 could lose power without warning and coast to a halt. Find out from your Mercedes dealer if yours is affected because it'll need to have an update performed to prevent this from happening. Vehicle may cut out This recall is different from the previously mentioned one and involves an issue where the rear seat bench affects the electrical wiring for the fuel pump that lives under the back seats. This means that the fuel supply can be cut to the engine and cause it to stall. It affects E-Class' manufactured from the start of production until 31 August 2016. Is a used Mercedes E-Class saloon reliable? The current version of the E-Class finished in an excellent third place out of nine cars in the luxury car class in our most recent What Car? Reliability Survey. Mercedes-Benz as a brand finished a disappointing 24th out of 30 manufacturers in the same survey. If you'd like to see the full reliability list, head to the What Car? Reliability Survey pages for more information. What Car? has cars in stock Find out more Follow What Car? on our social channels Quick search All car reviews All new car deals Used cars for sale Leasing deals All used makes Vans and commercial vehicles New car awards Used car awards Autocar Classic & Sports Car Move Electric Tools & services Car finance Car warranty Gap insurance Sell your car Car Leasing Car Valuation Company car tax calculator Van tax calculator Legal bits Terms & conditions Cookie policy Privacy policy Complaints Information About What Car? Sitemap Contact What Car? Subscribe to our newsletter Subscribe to What Car? magazine What Car? is part of Haymarket Automotive , a division of Haymarket Media Group Haymarket Media Group 2025\", 'images': [], 'rank': 2}, {'url': 'https://www.motoreasy.com/mercedes-reliability/e-class', 'content': \"Are Mercedes E-Clas